nst the $15.00 cap. That includes two small ETH gas bridges ($1.40 each) because rh1 and arb1 started with 0 ETH. Both wallets that still hold funds keep far more than the gas for one more transaction.","outcome":{"kind":"target_reached"},"balances":{"eth1":{"ETH":"46500000000000000","WBTC":"0","USDC":"0"},"rh1":{"ETH":"50046533333333333","WBTC":"0"},"arb1":{"ETH":"813333333333333","WBTC":"0","USDC":"147699600"}},"in_transit_legs":[]},"id":"toolu_01TVBVgP1SWuVsq6efxDDYeg"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":95,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"reported\":true}","toolCallId":"toolu_01TVBVgP1SWuVsq6efxDDYeg","toolName":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_report_result","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":96,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The swap and split are done. All seven legs confirmed, and nothing is still in transit.\n\n- **Ethereum wallet (eth1):** swapped 0.1 ETH into 495,000 WBTC units (0.00495 WBTC), then bridged half to each destination. It has 0.0465 ETH left and no WBTC.\n- **Robinhood Chain wallet (rh1):** received 246,666 WBTC units and swapped them to ETH. It now holds about 0.0500 ETH (50,046,533,333,333,333 wei), including some ETH I bridged over for gas.\n- **Arbitrum wallet (arb1):** received 246,666 WBTC units and swapped them to 147.6996 USDC. It also holds 0.000813 ETH left over from the gas bridge.\n- **Cost:** $10.2208 total, under your $15.00 cap. I bridged 0.001 ETH to each of rh1 and arb1 (about $1.40 each) because both started with 0 ETH and couldn't pay gas for their swaps. Swapping to USDC on Ethereum and bridging that would have cost about $5.30 for the Arbitrum half, so this route was cheaper."}]}],"completeness":{"transcriptCaptureComplete":true,"modelObservedTruncation":false,"auxiliarySourceComplete":true,"finalAnswerPresent":true,"nativeVisibleEvidenceAvailable":true},"gaps":[],"publication":{"kind":"public_redacted","sourceConversationSha256":"204f2acc92fd8f0e9eb518be7eec77f66f2aded54aabcc32986f87cbcbf343f0","redactions